{"type":"thinking","text":"We have rsvg-convert supports SVG animation? It renders static, not CSS animations maybe initial. Could use convert? only rsvg. Maybe node puppeteer? Check. But primary task create SVG. Need design.\n\nLet's plan scene dimensions 900x650 perhaps landscape. Warm background with coastal theme maybe pelican on bicycle along boardwalk, sky gradient, sun, clouds, sea. Animation: bicycle moving across? User specifically wheels and cranks moving, pelican active. Could make background scrolling to imply movement, wheels rotating, crank rotating, pelican legs pedaling. A pelican sits on saddle (body above saddle, wings maybe holding handlebars), feet on pedals. Need anatomically recognizable pelican: huge beak with pouch, white/cream body, black wing tips, short legs. Riding bicycle. Animation include pedaling legs and wheels, crank. We can do a side view. Face right, bicycle heading right. Saddle under body. Wings extending to handlebar grips. Maybe pelican wears small helmet/scarf? Keep cute. Need animation smooth loop.\n\nImportant: mechanical correctness: crank central at bottom bracket, chainring, chain to rear hub, pedals attached to crank at opposite ends, legs from hip to pedals. Animating legs with IK is tricky in pure SVG/CSS. Could approximate with two-segment legs using nested groups at hip and knee with synchronized rotations. Or simpler: use SMIL animateMotion? Pure SVG animation via CSS rotations. Need pedals/cranks rotating. Legs must be attached to pedals visually. Could construct each leg as two line segments with joint keyframes computed for angles across cycle. Hard but doable manually. Maybe use <animate> on leg segments with values. Need ensure feet match pedals. Or could have pelican's legs not connected and just animate feet? Better design cover legs subtly with body? But user says actively riding, not necessarily pedaling? Yet cranks moving, likely pedaling. To sell it, legs need move.\n\nCould use JavaScript inside SVG to compute IK for legs, set transforms, animate via requestAnimationFrame. But animated SVG may need scripting permitted. CSS/SMIL more portable. Could use SVG SMIL and computed keyframes. Let's do pure SVG with JS? User asked animation, file .svg. Animations via CSS/SMIL are embedded and autoplay. JS works in browser but fails in static preview maybe. Better pure SVG CSS/SMIL. We can use CSS animations on wheels/crank/pedals and legs with appropriate transforms. Need accurate enough.\n\nDesign frame:\nCanvas viewBox 0 0 1000 700. Background:\n- soft sky gradient peach/blue.\n- sun.\n- distant ocean with waves.\n- clouds drifting.\n- boardwalk road under bicycle, speed lines moving left.\n- foreground plants.\n\nBicycle:\n- Wheels: rear center (350, 520), front center (690, 520), radius 105. Tires black/dark teal stroke ~14, rims gold, spokes.\n- frame: teal/coral? Let's choose vintage bicycle with deep teal frame and cream accents. Rear hub (350,520), front hub (690,520), bottom bracket (510,525) maybe too close to ground? Wheel radius 105, ground 625, BB at 510, 525? Crank radius 32 => pedals y 493-557, above ground. Seat tube up from BB to saddle at (420,360), top tube to head tube (630,375), down tube to head. Front fork from hub to head tube. Handlebars around (650,335). Rear stays.\n\nPelican sits at saddle around (430, 330): large white body ellipse tilted, tail left, neck rising/leaning forward toward handlebar, head around (600, 220), huge beak forward/right (to 760,240) with pouch. Wing reaches toward handlebar grips (645,330). Maybe wing is on near side, we see one wing curving to handlebar. Feet on pedals.\n\nNeed overall composition. Pelican body occupies upper middle, bike lower. Beak distinctive. Eye, crest feathers maybe.\n\nAnimation:\n- wheels: rotate full 360 over e.g. 1.3s around hub. Spokes lines in group centered at 0,0 with transform via CSS. Better define each wheel as <g transform=\"translate(cx cy)\"><g class=\"wheel\">... spokes centered 0,0, tire etc.</g></g>. Wheel rotation animation.\n- crank: central at (510,525), crank arms + pedals. Could animate crank group rotate 360 over 1.2s. Pedals should stay horizontal: attach counter-rotation on each pedal group. Since crank rotates, pedal position rotates. We can group crank arms with circles and each pedal group at crank radius; apply counter rotation to keep horizontal. Need CSS variables? Transform-origin issue. We can create <g class=\"crank\" style=\"transform-origin: 510px 525px\"> containing two arms and pedal groups. Pedal groups each at specific location and counter animation `transform: rotate(...)` with transform-origin local? If within rotating parent, child rotate inverse around its own center. Use nested: <g class=\"pedal-counter\" style=\"transform-origin: ...\"> with animation reverse; but transform origin has to be within local coordinates. In SVG CSS transform-origin coordinate relative? If style transform-origin: 0 0 on sub group translated? Hmm SVG CSS transforms can be finicky, but rsvg supports? Static screenshot only first frame anyway. Browser works.\n\nAlternative use SMIL <animateTransform> with values and transform origins manually. For wheel group centered at 0,0: animateTransform type=rotate from 0 0 0 to 360 0 0 dur=... repeatIndefinite. This is robust and no CSS origin complexities. Crank group at translated center: nested group `<g transform=\"translate(510 525)\"><g><animateTransform type=rotate .../>` so origin 0,0. For pedals counter-rotate: each pedal assembly is at point (0,r) then `<g transform=\"translate(0,r)\"><g><animateTransform type=rotate values=\"0; -360\" ... /> <rect.../></g></g>`; because parent rotates, inverse keeps level. Solid.\n\n- Chain: movement indicated maybe dashed stroke chain with animate stroke-dashoffset. Could draw chain loop as path and animate dash offset. Use chain lines between chainring at 510,525 radius 33 and rear hub 350,520 radius 14. Draw upper/lower tangent path, dashed stroke. Animate stroke-dashoffset. Nice.\n\n- Legs: Use groups with animateTransform. Alternatively, could compute IK keyframe values manually at several phases and use animateTransform on thigh and shin. This is complicated but possible with script generating values.\n\nCould instead use JS inside SVG to compute leg joint positions every frame. But pure SMIL desirable. Another trick: Legs as curved shapes attached at hip and foot, updated via `values` attribute for path d? SVG SMIL animate on d not universally supported? `<animate attributeName=\"d\" values=\"...\">` supported in browsers for simple path with same commands. Could generate numerous path d keyframes for leg from hip to pedal, bending forward appropriately. Maybe easier: thigh+shin segments with rotations. For each phase, compute hip, pedal, knee via 2-link IK. Then thigh angle = atan2(knee-hip), shin angle = atan2(pedal-knee). We can use `<g transform=\"translate(hip) rotate(angle)\"> <line...> <g transform=\"translate(thighLength,0) rotate(angle2-angle1)\"> ...`. Animate rotation values linearly between milestones. Use 8 or 12 keyframes. SMIL rotation values with calcMode linear. Need smooth continuity near wrap 360. Compute angles avoiding wrap. Could use 20 points. But SVG's animateTransform values interpolation linearly in angle numeric, can handle. As long as angle change no jumps. We can calculate.\n\nActually simpler with JS to derive from crank angle each animation frame; but SMIL should work. Let's compute exact coordinates and animate rotations. Because origin at hip and lengths, rotation angle measured from +x axis. Need design hip position around (430, 400). Pedal motion center (510,525), crank radius 35. For near leg and far leg 180 out of phase. Hip maybe (425,405). Leg lengths: thigh 75, shin 85. Distance hip to pedal at max? Hip (425,405), pedal range around (475-545, 490-560): dist from 110 to 174. Total leg 160, so at far bottom 174 impossible. Need set hip lower/legs longer or hip closer. Pelican sits on saddle at y=370; hip around 390. Legs short but can be long-ish. Let's compute with hip (440, 420), BB (515,525), crank radius 38. Max dist hip to pedal: sqrt((515-440+38)^2+(525-420+38)^2) around sqrt(113^2+143^2)=182. min dist ~sqrt(37^2+67^2)=76. Leg lengths total n","truncated":true}
