{"type":"thinking","text":"No ffmpeg/inkscape/chrome. rsvg can't animate. Could install? no network perhaps. But can use SVG animation and trust. Could also use a JS or custom renderer? Need visual check via static rendering of one or multiple keyframes. We can create static variant with transforms set at phases. Use rsvg-convert for raster and read_image. Good.\n\nNeed make impressive. Let's consider using an external SVG with CSS animations and script? Pure SMIL likely stable. But \"animation\" should animate in browser. Need add title/desc.\n\nLet's sketch coordinates carefully.\n\nCanvas 1000x700. Sky and ocean:\n- background rect gradient sky from #f8d8b0 at top? Maybe cheerful sunrise. Let's choose morning coastal: pale sky #F7E7D3 top to #CFEAF2 bottom, with warm sun #FFD27A, sea last 200px? But bicycle on boardwalk. Maybe scene:\n  - sky y 0-420 gradient cream to light blue.\n  - sun at (800,110) huge pale gold circle, subtle halo.\n  - distant sea y 360-480 in deep teal / blue, horizon at 380.\n  - boardwalk y 560-700? Bicycle ground at 640. Need background behind entire. Could set road/boardwalk path from y 550 to 700. Ocean from 340-550, beach? Bike on boardwalk, ocean behind. Ground line at 620 with wood planks.\n  - hills/land at horizon maybe.\n\nSet bike ground y = 630. Wheels radius 108, hubs y=522. So tire bottom 630. Rear (330,522), front (690,522), distance 360. BB at (500,530) between; chainstay etc.\n- Wheels radius 104 maybe in frame. Let's use hub rear (330,520), front (690,520), radius 105. Bottom y=625. Ground y=634 (small shadow). Bike wheelbase 360.\n\nFrame:\n rear hub A=(330,520)\n BB B=(505,527)\n front hub C=(690,520)\n seat cluster D=(418,365)\n head tube top E=(635,366), head bottom F=(656,425) maybe fork to front hub.\n top tube D->E (slight slope upward?).\n down tube B->F? Actually front fork/head. Let's set head tube from (628,356) to (655,420). Top tube from seat cluster (423,365) to head top (630,357). Down tube from BB (505,527) to head bottom (650,410). Seat tube from BB to seat cluster (423,365). Chain stays rear hub to BB. Seat stays rear hub to seat cluster. Front fork head bottom to front hub. Handlebars stem from head top up to (640,335), bar grips.\n\nSeat: saddle from (400,348) to (455,350), under pelican.\n\nPelican:\n Body large oval centered maybe (430,315), rx 105 ry 75, rotated -10deg? Body rear at x=320, front at x=540. Saddle at y=355 below belly. Body bottom ~385. Tail sticking left/up from (340,310) maybe.\n Neck rising from front body (500,280) to head (615,205); pelican neck thick curved. Could create path with cubic curves, white, warm shadow.\n Head center (622,200) radius 38; beak huge extending to x=815, y=215, with pouch curving under to y=275 and back to head. Beak coral/orange gradient, pouch pale pink/orange.\n Eye at (637,188) black/amber.\n Crest small feathers at back of head (590,165) maybe.\n Wing near side: from shoulder (465,295) curves to (610,345) handlebar grip, layered feathers. Need make it obviously a wing reaching handlebar. Shape shaped like wing: primary feathers extend back? If wing actively gripping handlebar, maybe folded wing with tip extending to grips. Use wing composed of 3 feathers along top. Colors off-white with gray/blue tips. Actually pelican wings are large, black-tipped. Could have wing stretch forward to handlebar (near wing) and a second wing maybe behind visible slightly. We can draw near wing as a curved shape from shoulder to grip and feathers trailing back slightly. Maybe easier: wing extends forward/down to handlebar, with visible primary feather fingers wrapping around grip. Use path body. But handlebar at (625,335) near head. Pelican body front at (520,315), wing can extend to (645,342).\n Far wing not needed or tucked.\n\n Legs: Hip maybe (455,380) hidden under body. Near leg (right side) visible orange with webbed foot on near pedal; far leg darker and on far pedal, drawn behind bike/crank? We'll draw far leg behind body/crank with darker orange, near leg over crank. Saddle is at y=350 so hip under body. Legs from (450,375) maybe. But if hip too high, distance to bottom pedal >... Let's recalc using hip H=(450,385), BB=(505,527), crank radius=38. Bottom pedal (505,565): dist=sqrt(55^2+180^2)=188.2. Thigh=110, shin=100 total 210. Fine. Top pedal (505,489): dist=sqrt(55^2+104^2)=117.6. Good. Max at rightmost? (543,527): dist sqrt(93^2+142^2)=169.7. Fine. Knees will work.\n\nFar leg hip maybe (445,383), offset phase 180. Need layer: far leg drawn behind bicycle frame and crank? Pedal at far side. Crank arms rotate. Order:\n- background\n- bike rear wheel/front wheel (wheels)\n- chain\n- far crank arm + far pedal, far leg maybe in front of far crank? A human leg on far side would be behind frame but visible. Put far leg before frame, then frame, then near leg and near crank. But far pedal under foot. Simpler draw both legs and cranks on top of frame; viewer doesn't mind. Maybe far leg darker and under near leg.\n- frame\n- body+neck+head etc.\n- near leg over frame and near crank.\n- wing over body to handlebar.\n- chainring maybe near side above crank.\n\nBut bike frame needs partly visible beneath pelican. Fine.\n\nAnimation:\n- wheels and crank rotate.\n- Legs thigh/shin rotations computed to track pedals.\n- Body bounce subtle: group animateTransform translate values 0 0; 0 -3; 0 0 during one crank cycle. Also head/neck bob.\n- Beak pouch jiggle maybe subtle scale.\n- Scarf? Add fluttering scarf maybe red, tied neck, trailing behind. Could animate two tails waving via CSS path? Or use animateTransform rotate on scarf ends group around (520,250), slight. Cute. But pelican already recognizable.\n- Background clouds drift slowly, sea waves.\n- Speed lines behind bike animating horizontally. Boardwalk planks scrolling? Since bicycle stays in place, moving ground planks/background communicates motion. Animate repeat groups within pattern? Can make boardwalk planks with CSS transform translate from 0 to -120 on group inside clip. Or use <pattern> with animation? Simpler group of lines with animateTransform translate, 0; -120. Duplicate across 1200 width. Same for sea sparkles.\n- Maybe little dust puffs at rear wheel.\n- Front basket with fish? Pelican riding to get fish. Add small wicker basket on handlebar with fish tail. Cute but complexity. Could add fish in basket. But user asks pelican actively riding. A basket with fish would be charming. Still main.\n\nNeed animation speed: wheel circumference ~660 px; if 1.1s per rotation looks fast. Bicycle ride moderate. 1.6s/rev wheel, crank maybe 1.2s (pedaling cadence 50 rpm) but wheel gearing should be faster than crank (2.5x). Wheels 1.2s, crank 3s? User specifically says moving; visible. Crank 1.6 sec maybe fast. Cycle should sync legs with crank. Set crank dur=1.8s; wheels dur=0.9s? That's 3x faster, physically plausible (gear ratio 2.5). But wheel 0.9s is fast; background scroll speed. Crank 1.8 s at 33rpm somewhat slow but visual. Could use crank 1.4s, wheel 0.7s too fast. For aesthetically pleasing, use crank 2.2 sec (27rpm) and wheel 1.1 sec. To show pedaling. Hmm. Better 1.8 crank, 0.9 wheel. Loop background every 1s.\n\nSMIL timing must align: wheel and ground both 0.9s. Legs keyframes over crank 1.8s. Body bounce 0.9s (two bobs per crank rev maybe). Chain 0.45s. If animations start same time (begin=\"0s\"), okay.\n\nLeg IK with crank period. Need generate rotate values. Note coordinate system y down. Angles: atan2(dy,dx) measured clockwise from +x. SVG rotate positive clockwise (because y down). Standard. For a thigh group at hip: <g transform=\"translate(H)\"> <g><animateTransform type=rotate values=\"a0;...;a0\" dur=1.8s.../> Then a line from 0,0 to L,0. The actual endpoint rotation positive with +x etc, yes.\n\nThen at knee, we need shin relative angle = beta - alpha (rotation in parent's rotated frame), where beta is absolute angle of shin. Nested `<g transform=\"translate(L,0)\"><g><animateTransform type=rotate values=\"(b-a)... \"/>...`. But careful: nested group rotates around knee after translation in parent rotated frame. Works.\n\nLeg styling: Thigh thick cream path/skin. But if only rotating line, thigh can be a rounded line with feather tufts. Use <path d=\"M0,0 Q...\">? A tap","truncated":true}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_rlYc6t3At7XGkbvfDUju5563","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport math\nBB=(505,527); r=38\n# thigh, shin lengths\nlegs={\n 'near': {'H':(452,378),'L1':100,'L2':95},\n 'far': {'H':(442,374),'L1':102,'L2':97},\n}\nN=24\nfor name,cfg in legs.items():\n    H=cfg['H']; L1=cfg['L1']; L2=cfg['L2']\n    phase=0 if name=='near' else math.pi\n    alphas=[]; rels=[]; knees=[]; feet=[]\n    for i in range(N+1):\n        th=2*math.pi*i/N\n        foot=(BB[0]+r*math.sin(th+phase), BB[1]+r*math.cos(th+phase)) # crank local (0,r): after rotation theta clockwise: (x,y)=(r sinθ, r cosθ) (since rotate: x'=r sinθ,y'=r cosθ)\n        target=(foot[0], foot[1]-10)\n        dx=target[0]-H[0]; dy=target[1]-H[1]\n        d=math.hypot(dx,dy)\n        d=min(d,L1+L2-0.01)\n        a=(L1*L1-L2*L2+d*d)/(2*d)\n        h=math.sqrt(max(0,L1*L1-a*a))\n        ux=dx/ math.hypot(dx,dy); uy=dy/math.hypot(dx,dy)\n        # base relative to actual d; use target direction but if clamped ignore\n        base=(H[0]+a*ux, H[1]+a*uy)\n        # perp to right/up\n        px=-uy; py=ux\n        # choose knee forward: compare +x alternatives\n        k1=(base[0]+h*px, base[1]+h*py)\n        k2=(base[0]-h*px, base[1]-h*py)\n        knee = k1 if k1[0] > k2[0] else k2\n        alpha=math.degrees(math.atan2(knee[1]-H[1],knee[0]-H[0]))\n        beta=math.degrees(math.atan2(target[1]-knee[1],target[0]-knee[0]))\n        # unwrap\n        if alphas:\n            while alpha-alphas[-1]>180: alpha-=360\n            while alpha-alphas[-1]<-180: alpha+=360\n        rel=beta-alpha\n        if rels:\n            while rel-rels[-1]>180: rel-=360\n            while rel-rels[-1]<-180: rel+=360\n        alphas.append(round(alpha,2)); rels.append(round(rel,2)); knees.append((round(knee[0],1),round(knee[1],1))); feet.append((round(target[0],1),round(target[1],1)))\n    print(name)\n    print('alpha=', ';'.join(map(str,alphas)))\n    print('rel=', ';'.join(map(str,rels)))\n    print('dmax', max(math.hypot(f[0]-H[0],f[1]-H[1]) for f in feet))\n    print('knees',knees[:4])\nPY","description":"Compute leg IK keyframes for pedaling"}}
