rom (505,527) to (654,411) passes behind chainring; at x=540, y=500. The foot at (505,479) extends right to (540,480), exactly along the down tube, likely visible as orange patch at (540,480) in full. Looks like a foot resting on the down tube rather than pedal? Hmm the pedal at (505,489), chainring at 527. Foot at top position will collide visually with the seat tube / top tube / down tube. In real bike, pedal at top is in front of frame (near side), so that's correct. But because foot extends forward, it overlays the down tube and looks like an orange blob. That's acceptable if animated.\n\nCould redesign pedal/foot orientation so foot extends less forward, maybe more compact webbed foot (x -5..22 instead of 35) to reduce overlap. Feet in image seem large. We can shorten foot to 26px and less thick. The foot at t=0 looked okay. At top, a smaller foot would clutter less.\n\nAlso the far foot at t=0 top was also visible under body. Fine.\n\nPerhaps move the bicycle **BB lower**? It's already low. Or raise body/legs? no.\n\nNeed check if leg animation is smooth. With 24 keyframes and linear, yes. But the animated positions we freeze show the thigh white pole ends at knee. The thigh is 110px long, shin 101. In t=.9, white thigh extends forward 100px, very visible and flat. Refine shape.\n\nLet's improve:\n1. Thigh shape: Tapered, shorter-looking with a feathered top and slight curve. Could make it mostly covered by body by raising hip? Hip at body bottom. Maybe draw thigh in two parts: a feathered upper leg (cream) with dark outline, plus a thin orange \"tarsus\" from knee to foot. The thigh itself can be curved. Since we rotate a group, shape can be curved path with length 110. We can make it asymmetric: broad at top (28px) tapering to 8px at knee, with a curved lower edge and feather notches. Add 3 small feather scallops along upper edge. This will read as a plump feathered thigh, not a pole. \n- `M 0 -15 C 30 -18 70 -14 110 -5 L110 4 C 70 11 35 12 0 12 Z` still similar. Make bend: `M 0 -15 C 25 -17 60 -12 110 -4 L110 4 C 65 6 30 9 0 13 Z`. The lower edge curves upward. Maybe.\n- Add feather scallops along bottom edge using little arcs and shadow.\n- Add a dark hip patch to anchor at body.\nActually with rotation, shape oriented along x, so curved edges okay.\n\n2. Far leg should be clearly darker and maybe thinner. Fine.\n\n3. Foot smaller: reduce x max from 35 to 29, and shape more like webbed foot with 3 toes:\n`M -2 -10 C 3 -14 9 -14 14 -11 C 19 -9 24 -8 28 -6 C 25 -2 20 0 13 0 C 6 0 0 -2 -3 -5 Z`. This ends at x=28. Could add toe notches at x=22,26. Better.\n\n4. Maybe draw the near foot **after** the near leg to cleanly overlap the shin; currently foot drawn first so shin overlays ankle. That's okay. No change.\n\n5. Far/near hip positions perhaps move down 4px? They're under body. no.\n\n6. Body might be too high/its bottom too flat; pelican looks like afloat? In image body bottom overlaps saddle and saddle visible, fine.\n\n7. Add more pelican identity: distinctive **huge pouch** is there. Maybe add a tiny **fish tail poking from pouch**? That would be funny but not required. Could be charming: a little silver fish tail sticking out of pouch. But user asks pelican riding bike; fish in pouch implies it caught one. However might confuse as a tongue. Avoid.\n\n8. Make neck a bit shorter and head bigger? Pelican head currently 80px wide, beak huge. Looks good.\n\n9. Wing: The wing could be more clearly a wing, with layered feathers. It currently has some. Maybe add feather lines and dark tips. It's fine.\n\n10. Tail: Enhance so silhouette reads pelican. Add a fan of 3 tail feathers extending left/up from body, dark tips. Current tail hidden. We can draw tail after body? It would show over body. Better before body and make it extend further left. Move tail tip to x=250, y=255, with 3 pointed feathers. This will be visible outside body. Let's update tail path:\n```\n<path d=\"M340 310 C310 303 282 288 255 266 C275 274 294 276 311 276 C323 268 337 269 349 277 C342 284 337 294 340 310 Z\" .../>\n```\nIt extends to x=255, visible. Add dark gray tips at tip? Pelican tail white. Maybe subtle gray tips. Add 3 pointed shapes:\n`M263 271 C277 279 291 282 305 280 C295 287 283 289 271 284 Z` etc. This might look like tail feathers.\nThe body rear starts x=326, so tail portion x=255..340 visible. Good.\nMaybe tail should angle upward, nice for motion.\n\n11. Background: currently the beach and deck static. Motion will show. Good.\n12. The sun has no subtle animation; fine.\n13. Boardwalk seams at t=.45 moved 75 px (could be seen), good.\n\n14. Scene clipping grass outside boardwalk? The left grass is in front of wood. Good.\n\n15. The bike front wheel is close to grass on right, fine.\n\n16. Does bicycle \"move\" visually? Boardwalk seams move left, body bobs, wheels spin. We could add small **speed lines** behind rear wheel / bike to emphasize forward. The puffs at rear wheel are subtle. Add 3 wind streak curved lines under the pelican/tail or above rear wheel. Animate translate. Could improve. Let's add \"motion swooshes\" at left behind bike:\n```\n<g stroke=\"#F9F2DE\" stroke-width=3 opacity=.5 linecap=round>\n <g><animateTransform translate 30,0 -> -30? ...\n <path d=\"M175 430 C200 427 223 428 245 433\"/>\n...\n</g>\n```\nBut static freeze would show. They could be mistaken for scribbles on sea. Place at y=390 and 470 behind bike. Perhaps not needed; boardwalk moving enough. Could add small dust puffs already. No.\n\n17. The bicycle's rear wheel is at x=320, but the saddle/body at x=420 means body is shifted forward. Center of gravity okay. The pelican rear/tail over rear wheel. good.\n\n18. The far leg appears as a third \"stick\" leaving the body at a strange location? It starts at x=442,y=352 (slightly left of near hip), under body, and extends. Fine.\n\n19. Need check z-order: Wing is after body and covers scarf tail. In image, the red scarf tail over body is visible but only the upper.