screen y 479 -> crop y 298 yes. It is directly behind the near shin at y~? near shin at y 479 is around x≈503, so same spot. That's an unfortunate overlap at t=0: near shin passes through far foot. The near shin is drawn over, obscuring. At other phases less. To avoid, maybe make near shin thinner or far foot smaller/darker. Or change the timing? At t=0, near foot at bottom, far foot at top. Near shin crosses through the far foot? Far foot at (505,479) local extends right to x=534. Near shin from (501,454) to (503,555) vertical around x=502, so it overlaps the far foot's left/heel. Yes. This will happen at other phases too, but not severe.\n\nCould alleviate by offsetting the far leg and pedal slightly to the left/right (far side) in x? Real perspective: far crank is on the other side and could be drawn a few px left. But both pedals at same x. We can shift far crank/leg horizontally by -4px? It would still attach to BB but slight perspective. Pedal far foot could be shifted -3px. Not necessary.\n\nBetter: layer far leg behind the frame and body (it is), and color it significantly darker, so overlap isn't confusing. Also make near leg stand out.\n\nBut the bigger issue is visual leg length/proportion. The white thigh is still a big straight white shape. We can hide more of it under a \"feather apron\" from the body. Maybe extend body bottom slightly lower at hip sides to cover the top half of thigh. But then saddle hidden. Alternative: draw a subtle **wing/feather skirt** behind the thigh? Hmm.\n\nCould solve by changing pedaling pose so hip is lower and thigh shorter? If hip at y=390 and legs shorter, body needs to extend down to hip, hiding more. Body could be lowered by 20px (center 280? no). Current body bottom 352. If we move body/hip down to 380, body gets closer to top tube, maybe saddle is hidden. But we could lower the entire pelican and bike? The bike top tube at 355; body bottom 352 is just above. Lowering body 20 would overlap top tube/saddle and look seated better? Wait body bottom y=352 means it sits at saddle y=350. If lowered, it would intersect frame. So no.\n\nIn real cycling, the thigh emerges from body at hip and is about 2/3 of thigh visible. With a pelican body, legs are short but we lengthened to reach. It's okay. A cartoon can have long legs.\n\nMaybe make the thigh look more feathered by giving it a **scalloped feather skirt** at its upper edge and a gradient. The crop shows a plain cream bar with slight scallop lines at the lower edge but hard to see. Could add dark feather tips or a curved silhouette. Also taper more toward the knee. It already tapers, but crop shows a wide white bar. Let's make the top thicker and bottom much thinner, with a curved neck:\n`M0 -18 C24 -19 58 -14 110 -5 L110 5 C68 7 34 8 0 14 Z` currently at x=60 thickness ~20? Let’s visualize. The crop shows white thigh width about 20 at knee? Actually it appears 16px. Might be fine. The issue is color contrast: cream white against body. Could add a dark outline and a feather pattern.\n- Maybe color the thigh slightly darker (#EBDFCC) and add 3-4 scallop cuts at the bottom edge with small notches. This will read as a feathered leg.\n- Add a ring of feathers at hip and a small orange \"knee\" joint.\n- Could put a narrow orange line along the thigh underside to imply skin.\n\nAlternatively, model the leg as a **single thick orange leg** with a feathered upper section (body-colored) only around hip, and an orange lower leg. Current knee joint at ~454 is midway. If we make the thigh orange as well, the entire leg becomes a long orange line, more bird-like but might be too thin and long. Hmm.\n\nCould make the visible thigh shorter by placing the knee higher and using a three-segment leg? The knee is determined by IK with thigh 110. If we shorten thigh and lengthen shin, knee would be higher (closer to hip) and shin longer. That might look better: the visible white thigh would be shorter, orange shin longer. For instance, thigh 65, shin 150 (total 215). Then knee is much closer to hip; the long orange tarsus dominates. This is more bird-like! Let's consider.\n\nBird anatomy: femur short, hidden; tibiotarsus long; tarsometatarsus long. In side view, a bird's leg is mostly long thin orange, with a feathered thigh near body. So use L1=60 (thigh), L2=155 (shin) total 215. IK: knee lies between hip and foot such that distances. For near at bottom target (505,555), d~207. The knee position with L1=60, L2=155: a=(3600-24025+d²)/(2d) ≈ (3600-24025+42849)/(414)=54.3; h=sqrt(3600-2948)=25.5; knee near hip, offset. So knee at ~H + 54 along line plus small perpendicular. White thigh short, orange lower leg long. This would look much more like a bird leg and less like a human thigh. Great idea. Need recompute keyframes and update path lengths. Also foot target same. Hip at 452,356. Knee will be ~490,410 at bottom, and orange shin from knee to foot. At top target d~? maybe 130, still okay; knee might be closer to foot? Need check reach. `L1+L2=215` > max 207.45. Good.\n\nBut with thigh 60, shin 155, the knee may bend in weird ways / cross. Need compute and inspect. Let's calculate sample positions and angles and reach. Also knee solution forward. This will make legs mostly orange, better. The thigh shape only 60px, mostly under body. Could hide it entirely and draw a small feathered \"thigh\" at hip. This seems better.\n\nLet's compute for L1=62, L2=150 (sum212). Near max 207.45; far max 214.45 with H far and target. Need far sum >214.45: L1=64, L2=153 sum217 (near L1=62,L2=150 sum212). Far max 214.45 <217. Good.\n- Near white thigh length 62, orange shin 150.\n- Far thigh 64, shin 153.\nAt t=0 near: hip (452,356), foot (505,555). d=207.45. Because near maximal extension (sum 212), knee roughly on line at distance 60 from hip. Knee ~ (468,413). Shin to foot (505,555) length 150. This looks like a long orange leg with a white thigh stub. Great. At t=.9 near foot top (505,479), d=?? H=(452,356), target (505,479) dx53 dy123, d=133.9. With L1=62,L2=150, knee solution forward maybe knee far out x? Let's compute. Could be knee at (508,390), shin down-left? Need see.\nFor far at t=0 target (505,479) from H=(442,352) dx63 dy127 d=141.8. L1=64,L2=153 sum217. Knee perhap","truncated":true}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_uVViO0isrlfAIfQb1GcU0252","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport math\nBB=(505,527); r=38\nlegs={\n 'near': {'H':(452,356),'L1':62,'L2':150,'phase':0},\n 'far': {'H':(442,352),'L1':64,'L2':153,'phase':math.pi},\n}\nN=24\nfor name,cfg in legs.items():\n    H=cfg['H']; L1=cfg['L1']; L2=cfg['L2']; phase=cfg['phase']\n    alphas=[]; rels=[]; maxd=0; knees=[]; feet=[]\n    for i in range(N+1):\n        th=2*math.pi*i/N\n        x = -r*math.sin(th+phase)\n        y = r*math.cos(th+phase)\n        target=(BB[0]+x, BB[1]+y-10)\n        dx=target[0]-H[0]; dy=target[1]-H[1]\n        d=math.hypot(dx,dy); maxd=max(maxd,d)\n        if d>L1+L2-0.01: print('unreachable', name, i, d, L1+L2)\n        d=min(d,L1+L2-0.01)\n        a=(L1*L1-L2*L2+d*d)/(2*d)\n        h=math.sqrt(max(0,L1*L1-a*a))\n        ux=dx/math.hypot(dx,dy); uy=dy/math.hypot(dx,dy)\n        base=(H[0]+a*ux, H[1]+a*uy)\n        px=-uy; py=ux\n        k1=(base[0]+h*px, base[1]+h*py)\n        k2=(base[0]-h*px, base[1]-h*py)\n        knee = k1 if k1[0] > k2[0] else k2\n        alpha=math.degrees(math.atan2(knee[1]-H[1],knee[0]-H[0]))\n        beta=math.degrees(math.atan2(target[1]-knee[1],target[0]-knee[0]))\n        if alphas:\n            while alpha-alphas[-1]>180: alpha-=360\n            while alpha-alphas[-1]<-180: alpha+=360\n        rel=beta-alpha\n        if rels:\n            while rel-rels[-1]>180: rel-=360\n            while rel-rels[-1]<-180: rel+=360\n        alphas.append(round(alpha,2)); rels.append(round(rel,2)); knees.append((round(knee[0],1),round(knee[1],1))); feet.append((round(target[0],1),round(target[1],1)))\n    print(name,'maxd',round(maxd,2),'sum',L1+L2)\n    print('alpha=', ';'.join(map(str,alphas)))\n    print('rel=', ';'.join(map(str,rels)))\n    print('knee minmax', min(k[1] for k in knees), max(k[1] for k in knees))\n    print('knees0,6,12', knees[0],knees[6],knees[12])\nPY","description":"Compute IK with short feathered thigh and long tarsus"}}
