e orange leg may emerge from under; fine without.\n\nLet's darken far leg / foot. Use edits.\n- far shin outline #9A4F27 -> #7F3F20; inner #BE6E34 -> #A95B2E; knee #B3612E -> #935026.\n- far foot fill #C57238 -> #A75D32, stroke #9C4F26 -> #7F3F1F; toe lines same.\n- far thigh already #E1D3BF; darken to #D8C7AF / stroke #BEAA91.\n- far foot maybe draw with opacity .95.\n\nLet's do.\n\nAlso fix small possible issue: the **saddle appears under body but the near leg white thigh starts from body and path from hip under body, good.**\n\nNext, perhaps reduce **foot size** further? The near foot at t=.9 top looks like a large orange flipper sticking forward over down tube. It's okay cartoon. At crop, foot at top is at (505,479) extending right; down tube passes behind, foot visible. Fine.\n\nNeed maybe adjust **chainring center** and crank pedal feet: near foot at top overlaps chainring? no, top at 479 above chainring 527, good.\n\nNow about **body bob and wing**: wing is static and body moves 2.6px up. At t=.45 body up 2.6; wing shoulder static. Might look like body detaches slightly? tiny.\n\nPotential issue: **head and beak overly static** while body bobs; adds life? The whole body group bobs including head. fine.\n\nPotential issue: **neck shape** where it meets head: there is a visible thin line? Head overlaps. fine.\n\nPotential issue: **beak mouth** is huge and pouch full. Great.\n\nPotential issue: color contrast of beak and sun (both orange). The sun is far right above beak; okay.\n\nPotential issue: The **wing looks like a spread wing rather than folded**; it is extended to handlebar, fine. It has dark tips, layered feathers. Good.\n\nPotential issue: The **handlebar** is largely hidden by wing and neck, but the grip red end is visible. Bell. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: The **saddle** is barely visible but there. Could extend saddle nose more prominently to the right at x=480, and perhaps draw a silver seatpost visible below body. Current seatpost hidden by body/sad